.TH NULLFETCH 1 "2026-11-26" "nullfetch 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nullfetch \- tiny system fetch for Linux with terminal images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nullfetch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nullfetch
prints system information next to an ASCII logo or a terminal image. It uses
only the Python standard library; external image converters are optional.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-logo
Hide the ASCII logo.
.TP
.BR \-\-logo " " \fINAME\fR
Show the given logo: \fIauto\fR, \fInone\fR, or a name from \fBlogos.py\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-logo\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Use a custom ASCII art file.
.TP
.BR \-\-image " " \fIFILE\fR ", " \-\-image\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Show an image next to the system information.
.TP
.BR \-\-image\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Renderer: \fIauto\fR, \fIblocks\fR, \fIascii\fR, \fIkitty\fR, \fIiterm\fR,
\fIchafa\fR, \fIviu\fR, \fIjp2\fR, \fIimg2txt\fR, \fItimg\fR or \fIsixel\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-image\-width " " \fIN\fR ", " \-\-image\-height " " \fIN\fR
Image size in terminal cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-image\-position " " \fIP\fR
Place the image at \fIside\fR, \fItop\fR or \fIbottom\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-image\-bg " " \fICOLOR\fR
Color behind transparent pixels.
.TP
.BR \-\-accent " " \fICOLOR\fR
Accent color as a name, distribution name or \fB#rrggbb\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fIMODE\fR
Color mode: \fIauto\fR, \fIalways\fR, or \fInever\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Visual theme: \fIdefault\fR, \fImono\fR, \fIlight\fR, \fIneon\fR, \fIdark\fR,
\fInord\fR, \fIgruvbox\fR, \fIdracula\fR, \fItokyo\fR, \fIsolarized\fR or
\fImatrix\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Use a tighter visual layout.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Show every available module.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-fields
List module names and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-image\-modes
List image rendering modes and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-separator " " \fITEXT\fR
Text printed between a label and its value.
.TP
.BR \-\-bar\-width " " \fIN\fR
Width of RAM, swap and disk bars.
.TP
.BR \-\-bar\-style " " \fISTYLE\fR
\fIblocks\fR, \fIascii\fR, \fIarrows\fR, \fIdots\fR or \fIlines\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: \fItext\fR, \fIjson\fR, \fIcsv\fR, \fImarkdown\fR or
\fIoneline\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Ignore cached values and the image cache.
.TP
.BR \-\-cache\-ttl " " \fIN\fR
Lifetime of cached slow values in seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-network
Skip network modules.
.TP
.B \-\-timing
Print module collection time on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-save\-config
Save the selected appearance and modules as defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-config
Show saved defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-config
Remove saved defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-config
Write an example configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Change one value in the saved configuration.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use an alternate configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colors.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use ASCII-only bars, ellipsis and separators.
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Output width in columns.
.TP
.B \-\-oneline
Print one compact line for status bars.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-logos
List available logo names and exit.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-only " " \fIFIELDS\fR
Show only the given modules, comma separated.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print system information as JSON.
.SH FIELDS
Default: user, host, os, kernel, cpu, gpu, ram, disk.
.br
Extra: arch, uptime, cpu_cores, swap, disks, network, local_ip, public_ip,
battery, temperature, resolution, shell, terminal, de, wm, packages, processes,
locale, timezone, date.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-only cpu,ram
Show only the CPU and RAM lines.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-all
Show every module.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-image ~/wallpaper.png \-\-image\-position top
Show a PNG image above the information.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-format markdown \-\-only os,cpu,ram
Print a Markdown table.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-set theme=gruvbox
Change the saved theme.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colors when set to a non-empty value.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Directory containing \fInullfetch/config.json\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Directory containing cached values and rendered images.
.SH LICENSE
MIT
